A||||9||sailordude||Word to the Wise.  Don't try to get Air with a fiero!||||1||
Z||000000||sailordude||11-16-2001||06:52 PM||||Guys,<BR>  I don't know if any of you have tried to jump a bump or anything like that.  Well today I got that crazy thought in my head, so today I went to this railroad bump near by and tried to jump it. I got some air but when i came down I bottomed out.  I don't see any damage but the large "thud" didn't sound too good for the car.  So just a warning not to try.||||reg||1
Z||000001||85 gt fiero||11-16-2001||07:08 PM||||Duhhhh...... thats why i have skid plates. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-16-2001||07:11 PM||||Fieros have lots of sensitive alignment adjustments. Hopefully yours still goes down the road straight, dont pull to one side.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||11-16-2001||07:39 PM||||I wouldn't really recommend it either.  One of the guys at the tire place I go to used to have a Fiero and always talks to me about mine when I bring it in.  (I am there often too, the stock rims don't like holding air anymore!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  One day he was telling me how he loved to  jump rairoad tracks and stuff in it.  Did it all the time, until one day he found a rather steep railroad crossing.  He revved up the engine and peeled out towards this track... as the story goes... and got some serious lift out of it.  Unfortunately he didn't land straight and before he knew it he had flipped the Fiero and totalled it!  He wasn't hurt, but he swears he'll never jump a track again.<P>Can anybody see the moral of the story??  (and he was serious about it, so I believe him too!)||||reg||1
